{"title":"Clinical Researcher Roadmap","role":"Clinical Researcher","summary":"A Clinical Researcher with a BASLP background applies knowledge of audiology, speech-language pathology, communication sciences, and hearing disorders to research involving patients, clinical interventions, diagnostic technologies, rehabilitation methods, and healthcare outcomes.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Audiology & Speech-Language Pathology (BASLP)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Clinical Researcher with a BASLP background applies knowledge of audiology, speech-language pathology, communication sciences, and hearing disorders to research involving patients, clinical interventions, diagnostic technologies, rehabilitation methods, and healthcare outcomes."},{"type":"p","text":"This career is particularly suitable for graduates who want to move beyond direct clinical practice into evidence generation, clinical trials, academic research, medical-device research, rehabilitation research, and public-health studies."},{"type":"p","text":"Potential research areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Hearing loss"},{"text":"Cochlear implants"},{"text":"Hearing aids"},{"text":"Speech and language disorders"},{"text":"Voice disorders"},{"text":"Fluency disorders"},{"text":"Neurogenic communication disorders"},{"text":"Pediatric communication"},{"text":"Autism and communication"},{"text":"Dysphagia"},{"text":"Assistive communication technologies"},{"text":"Tele-audiology and tele-rehabilitation"},{"text":"Digital therapeutics"},{"text":"Clinical outcome research"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A Clinical Researcher may work in universities, hospitals, research institutes, medical-device companies, rehabilitation centres, CROs, public-health organizations, or clinical research programs."},{"type":"note","label":"Scope note","text":"“Clinical 